The latest MSTest is **4.2.3**. Here are the breaking changes relevant to your project:

## 1. `[ExpectedException]` is removed (compile error)

This is the biggest impact. Both your test methods using `[ExpectedException]` must migrate to `Assert.ThrowsExactly`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

## 2. `Assert.IsTrue(true)` triggers MSTEST0032 warning

In v4 this analyzer is elevated from Info → **Warning**. Your `Validate_ValidInput_Succeeds` test will produce a warning about an always-true assertion.

## 3. Other notable v4 changes (not directly hitting your code)

- `TestContext.Properties` is now `IDictionary<string, object>`
- `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed
- Assert message APIs no longer accept `params object[]` — use string interpolation
- Minimum TFM is .NET 8 (you're fine)
- Types hidden as internal, libraries must recompile

---

Would you like me to apply the upgrade to your project files?
